"README.md (384 bytes)\n     1→# greet-pkg\n     2→\n     3→A minimal Node.js package that exports a simple greeting function.\n     4→\n     5→## Install\n     6→\n     7→```bash\n     8→npm install greet-pkg\n     9→```\n    10→\n    11→## Usage\n    12→\n    13→```js\n    14→const { greet } = require(\"./index\");\n    15→\n    16→greet();        // \"Hello, world!\"\n    17→greet(\"Ada\");   // \"Hello, Ada!\"\n    18→```\n    19→\n    20→## API\n    21→\n    22→### `greet(name?)`\n    23→\n    24→Returns the string `Hello, <name>!`. Defaults to `\"world\"` when `name` is omitted.\n    25→\n    26→## License\n    27→\n    28→MIT\n    29→"